            <ArticleTitle>Emergency coronary stenting for acute occlusive dissection of the left main coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>227-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Catheter-induced left main coronary artery dissection is a rare but serious complication of diagnostic cardiac angiography. We report the case of a patient with mitral regurgitation and accidental dissection of the left main coronary artery successfully managed with intracoronary stent that allowed emergent surgical revascularization and mitral replacement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
